b36Ag2 solder: 179°C liquidus\n  - SAC0307 solder: 217°C liquidus\n  - SAC305 solder: 217°C liquidus\n  \nTAL Windows (observed from actual profiles):\n  - MINIMUM TAL required: 10-60 seconds\n    (Depends on solder alloy - LeadFree (SAC) needs 30-60s, Pb-Sn needs 10-30s)\n  \n  - MAXIMUM TAL allowed: 430 seconds\n    (To prevent thermal stress and component damage)\n  \n  - TYPICAL/OPTIMUM TAL: 60-150 seconds\n    (Best for joint reliability and thermal management)\n\nCalculation Method:\n  TAL = Time above liquidus temperature (linear interpolation)\n  Example: If liquidus = 183°C and reflow peak = 250°C\n  TAL is measured from first crossing above liquidus to final crossing below liquidus\n\"\"\")\n\nprint(\"\"\"\n3. PEAK TEMPERATURE\n===================\n\nMinimum Peak Temperature Requirement:\n  - For Sn63Pb37 (183°C liquidus): Minimum peak = ~210°C\n    (Minimum 20-30°C above liquidus, typically 240-245°C target)\n  \n  - For Sn62Pb36Ag2 (179°C liquidus): Minimum peak = ~205°C\n    (Minimum 20-30°C above liquidus, typically 235-240°C target)\n  \n  - For SAC0307/SAC305 (217°C liquidus): Minimum peak = ~250°C\n    (Minimum 30-40°C above liquidus, typically 245-260°C target)\n\nPeak Margin Above Liquidus:\n  From observed data:\n  - MINIMUM margin: 0.5°C (marginal, not recommended)\n  - RECOMMENDED margin: 20-40°C above liquidus\n  - TYPICAL/SAFE margin: 50-100°C above liquidus\n  - MAXIMUM: Limited by component thermal limits (typically 260°C max)\n\nPeak Dwell Time:\n  - Short dwell at peak: 0-30 seconds\n  - Excessive dwell (>30s) can cause component damage\n\"\"\")\n\nprint(\"\"\"\n4. CONVEYOR SPEED & DWELL TIME\n===============================\n\nHeated Oven Length:\n  - 8-Zone Oven: Effective heated length ≈ 180-200 cm (accounting for zone spacing)\n  - 10-Zone Oven: Effective heated length ≈ 220-250 cm\n  \nDwell Time Requirements:\n  - Minimum total time in oven: ~120 seconds (for fast profiles)\n  - Maximum total time in oven: ~600 seconds (to prevent thermal stress)\n  - Typical/Optimum: 180-400 seconds\n  \nConveyor Speed Calculation:\n  Speed (cm/min) = (Heated Length (cm) / Time in Oven (s)) × 60\n  \nObserved Conveyor Speeds from MES data:\n  - MINIMUM speed: 37.1 cm/min\n  - MAXIMUM speed: 106.7 cm/min\n  - TYPICAL range: 45-85 cm/min\n  \nSpeed vs. Oven Type:\n  - 8-Zone ovens: Typical range 45-95 cm/min\n  - 10-Zone ovens: Typical range 40-85 cm/min\n  - IR+Conv (hybrid) ovens: 37-106 cm/min (more flexible)\n\nDwell Time Example Calculations:\n  Assuming 200cm heated length:\n  - At 50 cm/min: (200 / 50) × 60 = 240 seconds ✓ Good\n  - At 37 cm/min: (200 / 37) × 60 = 324 seconds (slower, more time)\n  - At 106 cm/min: (200 / 106) × 60 = 113 seconds (fast, minimal time)\n\"\"\")\n\nprint(\"\"\"\n5. THERMOCOUPLE SELECTION & REPRESENTATIVE SENSOR\n==================================================\n\nTC Types Observed in Production:\n  Location options:\n    - largest_mass: thermal mass point (slowest heating)\n    - smallest_mass: thin area (fastest heating)\n    - board_edge: perimeter point\n    - center_BGA: BGA package center (critical)\n    - connector_shield: metal shield area\n    - near_heatsink: cooler thermal area\n\nHANDBOOK GUIDANCE - Representative Sensor Selection:\n  \n  COLD SPOT approach (most conservative):\n    - Monitor the largest_mass or slowest-heating location\n    - Set recipe to ensure even this cold spot reaches peak temp\n    - Guarantees all other points exceed peak requirement\n    - RULE: Minimum peak at cold spot = liquidus + 20-40°C\n  \n  HOTTEST SPOT approach (optimized):\n    - Monitor peak at hottest location (near_heatsink, smallest_mass)\n    - Risk: Cold spots may not reach required temperature\n    - Used with multiple TC validation or statistical process control\n  \n  IPC STANDARD (Recommended):\n    - Use 3-5 thermocouples on different board regions\n    - Report the MINIMUM peak temp observed across all TCs\n    - Ensure minimum peak >= liquidus + 20°C at ALL measurement points\n    - TAL measured at WORST (minimum) point\n\nPRODUCTION PRACTICE (from observed data):\n    - All 6 TCs monitored per production run\n    - Profile validation considers: largest_mass (cold spot), center_BGA, nearest heatsink\n    - Pass criteria: Min peak across all TCs >= required temp\n\"\"\")\n\nprint(\"\"\"\n6. BOARD GEOMETRY & BOARD-FAMILY SPECIFIC RULES\n===============================================\n\nBoard Families in Production:\n\"\"\")\n\nfor family in sorted(mes_df['board_family'].unique()):\n    family_data = mes_df[mes_df['board_family'] == family]\n    print(f\"\\n  {family}:\")\n    print(f\"    Sample board dimensions: {family_data['board_length_cm'].iloc[0]}cm x {family_data['board_width_cm'].iloc[0]}cm\")\n    print(f\"    Typical thickness: {family_data['board_thickness_mm'].iloc[0]:.1f}mm\")\n    print(f\"    Typical layers: {int(family_data['board_layers'].iloc[0])} layers\")\n    print(f\"    Typical mass: {family_data['board_mass_g'].mean():.1f}g\")\n    print(f\"    Thermal mass index: {family_data['thermal_mass_idx'].mean():.2f}\")\n\nprint(\"\"\"\n\nThermal Mass Impact Rules:\n  - Low thermal mass (< 0.7): Can use faster conveyor speeds (60-100 cm/min)\n  - Medium thermal mass (0.7-1.1): Use standard speeds (45-75 cm/min)  \n  - High thermal mass (> 1.1): Requires slower speeds (30-60 cm/min)\n  \nBoard-specific minimum peak temperatures:\n  - Wearable boards (high layer count): Liquidus + 50-80°C\n  - Mobile/RF boards (medium): Liquidus + 30-60°C\n  - Industrial CTRL (high mass): Liquidus + 20-40°C\n  - Sensor modules (small): Liquidus + 20-50°C\n\"\"\")\n\nprint(\"\"\"\n7. ZONE-SPECIFIC DEFINITIONS\n=============================\n\nStandard 8-Zone Oven Structure:\n  Zone 1: Preheat start (ambient to 100°C)\n  Zone 2: Preheat ramp (100-150°C)\n  Zone 3: Soak (150-200°C)\n  Zone 4: Thermal equilibration (180-200°C)\n  Zone 5: TAL transition (200-217°C liquidus)\n  Zone 6: Peak reflow zone (217-260°C)\n  Zone 7: Cooling ramp (descending 260-150°C)\n  Zone 8: Final cooling (150°C to ambient)\n\nStandard 10-Zone Oven Structure (more granular):\n  Zones 1-3: Preheat region (finer control)\n  Zones 4-5: Soak transition (prevent thermal shock)\n  Zone 6: Transition to peak\n  Zones 7-8: Peak reflow zone (longer dwell at peak)\n  Zones 9-10: Cooling (slower, prevents warping)\n\nZone Temperature Setpoints (from MES data):\n  - Preheat zones (1-3): 133-165°C\n  - Transition zones (4-5): 155-175°C\n  - Peak zones (6-7): 220-260°C\n  - Cooling zones (8-10): 150-250°C (descending)\n\"\"\")\n\nprint(\"\"\"\n8. KEY NUMERIC CONSTRAINTS SUMMARY\n==================================\n\nCRITICAL PARAMETERS (from handbook & observed practice):\n\nPreheat Region (25-150°C):\n  ✓ Ramp rate: 2-4°C/s (max 6°C/s allowed)\n  \nTAL (Time Above Liquidus):\n  ✓ Sn63Pb37: 60-150 seconds recommended, min 10s\n  ✓ Sn62Pb36Ag2: 60-150 seconds recommended, min 10s\n  ✓ SAC0307/SAC305: 30-150 seconds recommended, min 20s\n  ✓ Maximum: Never exceed 430 seconds\n  \nPeak Temperature:\n  ✓ Sn63Pb37 (183°C liq): 210-250°C (min 20°C, target 40-60°C above)\n  ✓ Sn62Pb36Ag2 (179°C liq): 205-245°C (min 20°C, target 40-60°C above)\n  ✓ SAC0307/SAC305 (217°C liq): 250-260°C (min 30°C, target 30-40°C above)\n  ✓ Max peak allowed: 260°C (component limit)\n  \nConveyor Speed:\n  ✓ Range: 37-107 cm/min\n  ✓ 8-Zone typical: 45-95 cm/min\n  ✓ 10-Zone typical: 40-85 cm/min\n  \nTotal Time in Oven:\n  ✓ Minimum: 120 seconds\n  ✓ Maximum: 600 seconds\n  ✓ Optimum: 180-400 seconds\n  \nCooling Rate:\n  ✓ Maximum cooling: Should not exceed 6°C/s (avoid warping)\n  ✓ Post-peak cooling: Gradual descent preferred\n\"\"\")\n\nPYTHON_EOF\n","description":"Generate comprehensive handbook extraction report"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1547,"cache_read_input_tokens":70329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1547,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"r